---
description: Keep repository searches and writes inside the user's specified project workspace.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Workspace boundary

- When the user specifies a workspace path, search, read, and write project files only inside that exact directory.
- Do not read, inspect, modify, or create files in Codex worktrees or any other checkout, even when files appear shared or identical.
- Do not switch the working directory to another checkout to recover, compare, or validate project changes.
- Leave the specified directory only when the user explicitly instructs you to create a new project elsewhere.
- Before file operations, verify the resolved path is under the specified workspace directory.
